  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "How to read the colors",
      "items": [
        "Grey/external = a human step (meeting, call, decision) or an outside system — not automated by this pipeline",
        "Teal/backend = an LLM agent reasoning alone; peach/messagebus = an LLM agent that also calls tools",
        "Gold/cloud = a deterministic tool or rule-based service — no LLM involved at all; violet/database = a data store",
        "In-Person Deep Dive's minutes feed Meeting Facilitator's post-meeting extraction (edge not drawn — crosses the data-source row; see agent-specifications.md)",
        "Notice Corpus Manager is peach/messagebus by role (LLM + tool call), but it's UI-triggered on-demand, not a persistent LangGraph agent (ADR-0029)",
        "Notice Corpus Manager's own edge into Notice Corpus (confirmed clauses become citable) is not drawn — crosses the whole diagram width for no added value; see agent-specifications.md",
        "Approval Coordinator is peach/messagebus, not gold/cloud (fixes Principal Engineer audit 1.5) — its guarded LLM summarize_feedback() call (ADR-0017) is real tool-calling LLM usage, the same reason Findings Author and Compliance Analyst are peach; it isn't a pure deterministic state tracker"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "violet",
      "title": "Human-in-the-loop",
      "items": [
        "Supervision-question list, findings/severity, and pre-AG submission require Lead/Approver sign-off",
        "AG-requested changes and LFI pre-exit concerns are routine revision loops, not rare edge cases",
        "Ungrounded verdicts fall back to human review. Personas/SLAs/observability: deployment diagram"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "slate",
      "title": "Three platform services not drawn as their own boxes here",
      "items": [
        "severity_rubric.lookup(), quant_analysis.compute(), and template_fill() each have a full input/output/timeout/retry contract in tool-contracts.md and are called by Findings Author (and quant_analysis.compute() also by Compliance Analyst for context) — omitted here to avoid three more boxes on an already-dense 12-component diagram",
        "Drawn as their own components with ownership tags in lfi-pipeline-deployment-v1.html instead, the diagram whose whole point is \"who owns and runs what\" (fixes Principal Engineer audit 1.2)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "emerald",
      "title": "Deferred to v2",
      "items": [
        "Content/plausibility validation agent",
        "Unified cross-feature review queue",
        "Effective-dated notice versions and SVF/other license types",
        "Card color key: emerald is reserved for \"deferred/out of scope\" across every diagram in this repo — never reused for an in-scope category (see the deployment diagram's cards)"
      ]
    }
  ]
